; Loaded after rules.egg when the Java analysis takes its bias, indicator and
; masked rows from these rules (EgglogPhase1, switched on with
; -DegglogPhase1=<egglog binary> or EGGLOG_PHASE1=<egglog binary>).
;
; An Intent row holds n and d as e-classes.  Java needs them as values of the
; method, so it names every value it wrote and asks which names the classes
; have.

; Val a t: t is the term of SSA value a.  A negative a names the product of
; the factors of the quotient call that defines value -a (a product the code
; never computes as one value).
(relation Val (i64 Term))

; IntentVal v a b c: an Intent row of site v whose n is the value a and whose
; d is the value b.  A class can hold several values, so one Intent row can
; give several of these; Java takes the first that site v's own expression
; reaches.
(relation IntentVal (i64 i64 i64 i64))
(rule ((Intent v n d c) (Val a n) (Val b d))
      ((IntentVal v a b c))
      :ruleset match)

; IntentSum v a1 a2 b c: an Intent row of site v whose n is the sum of the
; values a1 and a2.  Java uses it when n has no value of its own, as in
; (x + d - 1 + y) / d, where the code never computes x + y.
(relation IntentSum (i64 i64 i64 i64 i64))
(rule ((Intent v n d c) (= n (Add x y)) (Val a1 x) (Val a2 y) (Val b d))
      ((IntentSum v a1 a2 b c))
      :ruleset match)
